Based on your career interests in Industrial, Aerospace, and Electrical Engineering, and your strengths in Mathematics and Physics, here are three highly-ranked UK and EU universities offering relevant Bachelor's programs:

    Imperial College London (UK)[1][2]

+ Program: MEng Aeronautical Engineering (UCAS Code: H401)[3][4][5][6]

        Why it fits: This 4-year integrated Master's program directly addresses your interest in Aerospace Engineering. Imperial is consistently ranked among the top universities globally for engineering, particularly aerospace. The course provides a strong foundation in engineering principles, computational and analytical skills, aerodynamics, structures, propulsion, and flight mechanics, preparing you for careers in the aerospace industry.[3][4] The MEng qualification fully meets the educational requirements for becoming a Chartered Engineer (CEng).[3] Imperial also has top programs related to electrical and industrial engineering if your interests evolve.

    Delft University of Technology (TU Delft) (Netherlands - EU)

+ Program: BSc Electrical Engineering[7][8]

        Why it fits: TU Delft is one of Europe's leading technical universities, highly regarded for Electrical Engineering. This 3-year Bachelor's program covers a broad range of electrical engineering topics, including circuits, signals and systems, digital systems, telecommunications, and electrical energy, with a strong emphasis on mathematics and physics. It includes project work applying theoretical knowledge to practical designs, like building robots or chips.[8] While the primary language of instruction for the BSc Electrical Engineering is Dutch, many lectures and course materials are in English, and the university environment is very international. Note: TU Delft also offers a world-renowned BSc in Aerospace Engineering taught in English, which would be an excellent alternative.

    University of Cambridge (UK)[9][10]

+ Program: BA (followed by MEng) Engineering

        Why it fits: Cambridge offers a unique and prestigious Engineering program. The first two years provide a broad foundation across all major engineering disciplines (including mechanical, electrical, civil, etc.).[11] This allows you to explore different fields before specializing in the third and fourth years. You can choose to specialize in areas directly relevant to your interests, such as Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Electrical and Information Sciences, or Aerospace and Aerothermal Engineering.[11] There are also options related to manufacturing and management which align with Industrial Engineering concepts. This program leverages your strong maths, physics, and logical thinking skills, offering flexibility and leading to an integrated Master's degree (MEng) accredited by major engineering institutions.